{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Who joined.</b> They are the converts." "<b>And not pass.</b> A Jew is not authorized to transgress it." "<b>As written.</b> The meaning is that one reads the scroll, and because Ezra the Scribe divided the verses, and not many years later our Sages of blessed memory decreed that the reader not pause except at the end of a verse." "<b>Every year and year.</b> Simple or intercalated. And now he mentioned what the Jews upheld, as Mordecai wrote to impose upon them. And the meaning of 'these days are remembered and kept' to do so — all families and all provinces, lest a person think he is not obligated if he is in a place where there was no Jew in the days of the miracles, or in a new province."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:26.147073934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}